<title>CHILE: Chile reserves fall slightly to $15.19 bln in Oct.</title>
<headline>Chile reserves fall slightly to $15.19 bln in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's international reserves fell $75 million in October to $15.19 billion, the central bank said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>The drop is the result of a $74 million deficit in the balance of payments account and a $1 million reduction in the value of the reserves as the result of international currency fluctuations, said the bank.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
